              { title: 'Floyd’s Cycle Finding', text: 'Fast pointer moves 2 steps, slow pointer moves 1 step. If they meet, a cycle exists. Reset slow to head, move both 1 step; collision point is the cycle entry node.' },
              { title: 'Iterative Reversal', text: 'prev = null, curr = head. while (curr != null): next = curr.next; curr.next = prev; prev = curr; curr = next. Returns prev as new head in O(N) time and O(1) space.' },
              { title: 'Find Middle Node', text: 'Slow moves 1 step, fast moves 2 steps. When fast or fast.next is null, slow is at the exact middle (first mid for even length, exact mid for odd length).' },
              { title: 'LRU Cache Design', text: 'Doubly Linked List (maintains access order with head as Most Recently Used and tail as Least Recently Used) + HashMap (stores key -> Node for O(1) lookups and node splicing).' },
              { title: 'Merge K Sorted Lists', text: 'Insert head of each of the K lists into a Min-Heap (PriorityQueue). Extract min, append to result, and insert next node from the extracted list in O(N log K) time.' }
