              { title: 'Time & Work LCM Shortcut', text: 'Assume Total Work = LCM(days taken). Daily Efficiency = Total Work / Days. Combined Time = Total Work / Sum of Efficiencies.' },
              { title: 'Successive Percentage Formula', text: 'Net percentage change = a + b + (a * b) / 100. For discounts: net discount = d1 + d2 - (d1 * d2) / 100.' },
              { title: 'Time, Speed & Distance Rules', text: 'Convert km/h to m/s: multiply by 5/18. Average Speed for equal distance: (2 * S1 * S2) / (S1 + S2). Relative speed: (S1 + S2) opposite, (S1 - S2) same direction.' },
              { title: 'Probability Complement Rule', text: 'P(At least one success) = 1 - P(Zero successes). Vastly quicker than calculating sums of multiple combination scenarios in screening tests.' },
              { title: 'Circular Seating Logic', text: 'Fix first person at top position (symmetry). Facing Center: Left is clockwise, Right is anti-clockwise. Facing Outward: Left is anti-clockwise, Right is clockwise.' },
              { title: 'Syllogism Venn Diagrams', text: 'All A are B (A subset of B), Some A are B (overlap), No A are B (disjoint). Conclusion is only valid if it holds across ALL possible valid Venn diagrams.' }
