            interviewQuestions: [
              "Explain the mathematical premise of LoRA (Low-Rank Adaptation): W = W_0 + Delta W = W_0 + (alpha / r) * (B x A). Why does decomposition into rank r << d reduce trainable parameters by over 99%?",
              "What is QLoRA, and how do 4-bit NormalFloat (NF4) data type, Double Quantization, and Paged Optimizers enable fine-tuning 70B parameter models on consumer GPUs?",
              "Compare Post-Training Quantization (PTQ) techniques: AWQ (Activation-aware Weight Quantization), GPTQ, and GGUF (llama.cpp). What are the trade-offs between memory footprint and perplexity degradation?",
              "When should an enterprise choose Fine-Tuning versus Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)? In what scenarios is combining RAG + LoRA necessary?",
              "How does vLLM achieve high-throughput LLM serving using PagedAttention, and how does KV cache memory fragmentation degrade standard inference?"
            ],
            revisionNotes: [
              { title: 'LoRA (Low-Rank Adaptation) Math', text: 'W = W_0 + Delta W = W_0 + (alpha / r) * (B x A), where W_0 in R^(d x k), B in R^(d x r), A in R^(r x k) (r << d). A is initialized with Gaussian noise and B with zeros → Delta W = 0 at start.' },
              { title: 'QLoRA 4-bit Innovations', text: '1. NormalFloat4 (NF4): Information-theoretically optimal quantile quantization for normal distributions. 2. Double Quantization: Quantizes quantization constants to save 0.37 bits/param. 3. Paged Optimizers: Uses CPU paging on CUDA memory spikes.' },
              { title: 'Quantization Formats Comparison', text: 'AWQ: Protects 1% salient weights based on activation magnitude (best for GPU serving). GPTQ: One-shot second-order quantization. GGUF: CPU/Metal quant format for llama.cpp/Ollama.' },
              { title: 'RAG vs Fine-Tuning Decision Matrix', text: 'Use RAG to add dynamic factual knowledge, private document retrieval, and citation verification. Use Fine-Tuning (LoRA) to teach specific tone, formatting style, domain vocabulary, or structured syntax.' },
              { title: 'vLLM PagedAttention Concept', text: 'Standard LLM serving fragments KV cache memory up to 80%. PagedAttention divides the KV cache into non-contiguous virtual memory pages, enabling near-zero memory waste and 5x-10x batch throughput.' }
            ]
