                title: '4. Refresh Token Rotation & Theft Detection',
                text: 'When a refresh token is used to generate a new access token, the old refresh token is invalidated and replaced with a new one in the same token family. If an already-invalidated refresh token is submitted, the server detects token theft and immediately revokes all tokens in that family.',
