            "interviewQuestions": [
              "Explain the difference between Liveness, Readiness, and Startup Probes in Kubernetes. What happens to a Pod when each probe fails?",
              "Explain the difference between Resource Requests and Resource Limits. What happens when a Pod exceeds its CPU limit versus its Memory limit?",
              "How does Kubernetes determine Quality of Service (QoS) classes (Guaranteed, Burstable, BestEffort), and how does the node OOM score use QoS during eviction?",
              "How does a Rolling Update work in a Kubernetes Deployment? Explain the parameters maxSurge and maxUnavailable, and how they guarantee zero downtime.",
              "What is a PodDisruptionBudget (PDB), and why is it critical when draining Kubernetes nodes during cluster upgrades?",
              "What is Helm, and how does Helm templating (values.yaml, templates/, Chart.yaml) simplify managing multi-environment Kubernetes deployments?",
              "Walk through how you troubleshoot a Pod stuck in CrashLoopBackOff versus ImagePullBackOff versus Pending state."
            ],
            "revisionNotes": [
              {
                "title": "KEY DIFFERENCE: Liveness vs Readiness Probes",
                "text": "Liveness Probe: Checks if container is running; failure restarts the container. Readiness Probe: Checks if container is ready to accept traffic; failure removes Pod IP from Service Endpoints without restarting."
              },
              {
                "title": "RULE: CPU vs Memory Limit Exceeded",
                "text": "CPU is a compressible resource: exceeding CPU limit causes CPU throttling; Memory is non-compressible: exceeding Memory limit triggers immediate OOMKilled (Exit Code 137)."
              },
              {
                "title": "CONCEPT: QoS Classes",
                "text": "Guaranteed: requests == limits for all containers; Burstable: requests < limits; BestEffort: no requests or limits set (evicted first when node runs out of memory)."
              },
              {
                "title": "FORMULA: Rolling Update Parameters",
                "text": "maxSurge: maximum pods created above desired count during update; maxUnavailable: maximum pods that can be unavailable during update. Defaults: 25% each."
              },
              {
                "title": "COMMAND: Essential K8s Debugging Commands",
                "text": "kubectl describe pod <pod_name> (Check Events!); kubectl logs <pod_name> --previous (Check crash logs); kubectl get events --sort-by=.metadata.creationTimestamp."
              },
              {
                "title": "PRODUCTION NOTE: Helm Rollbacks",
                "text": "helm history <release> (View revision history); helm rollback <release> <revision_number> (Instantly roll back to previous stable release in seconds)."
              }
            ]
